{
  "dom_id": "step-e10088",
  "name": "Example: Using the CLT With a Population Whose Probability Distribution Is Discrete",
  "problem": "| $x$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.4$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.4$ |\n\nLet $X_1, X_2, \\ldots, X_{185}$ be a random sample of size $n = 185$ from a population with the probability mass function given above. Find an approximation in terms of $\\Phi(z)$ for $P(|\\overline{X}| \\gt 0.1).$\n\n*Note: $\\Phi(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution.*",
  "worked_solution": "Suppose that $X_1, X_2,\\ldots, X_n$ is a random sample of size $n$ from a population with population mean $\\mu$ and population standard deviation $\\sigma.$ The central limit theorem (or CLT) states that for sufficiently large $n,$ the distribution of the sample mean $\\overline{X}$ can be approximated as \n\n$$\n\\overline{X}\\sim N\\!\\left(\\mu,\\frac{\\sigma^2}{n}\\right).\n$$\n\nIn our case:\n\n- the sample size is \n\n$$\nn = 185,\n$$\n\n- the population mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mu  & =\\text{E}[X] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}f({x}_{i}) \\\\  & =-3\\cdot 0.4+(-1)\\cdot 0.1+1\\cdot 0.1+3\\cdot 0.4 \\\\  & =-1.2-0.1+0.1+1.2 \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- the population variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =((-3)^{2}\\cdot 0.4+(-1)^{2}\\cdot 0.1+{1}^{2}\\cdot 0.1+{3}^{2}\\cdot 0.4)-{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(3.6+0.1+0.1+3.6)-0 \\\\  & =7.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by the CLT, we have that the distribution of the sample mean can be approximated as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{X} & ∼N\\,(\\mu ,\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n}) \\\\  & ∼N\\,(0,\\frac{7.4}{185}) \\\\  & ∼N(0,0.04).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to find $P(|\\overline{X}| \\gt 0.1).$ So, we convert $\\overline{X}$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(|\\overset{―}{X}|>0.1) & =P(\\overset{―}{X}<-0.1)+P(\\overset{―}{X}>0.1) \\\\  & ≈P(Z<\\frac{-0.1-0}{\\sqrt{0.04}})+P(Z>\\frac{0.1-0}{\\sqrt{0.04}}) \\\\  & =P(Z<-0.5)+P(Z>0.5) \\\\  & =P(Z<-0.5)+1-P(Z<0.5) \\\\  & =1+Φ(-0.5)-Φ(0.5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy the symmetry of the normal distribution, we have\n\n$$\n\\qquad \\Phi(-0.5) \n= 1-\\Phi(0.5).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(|\\overset{―}{X}|>0.1) & =1+Φ(-0.5)-Φ(0.5) \\\\  & =1+(1-Φ(0.5))-Φ(0.5) \\\\  & =2-2Φ(0.5) \\\\  & =2(1-Φ(0.5)).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-e10088\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block;\">\n    \n                 \n                <div class=\"example\">\n                    <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                        <div class=\"stepName\"><span class=\"stepType\">Example:</span> Using the CLT With a Population Whose Probability Distribution Is Discrete</div>       \n                        <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"e10088\">?</div>\n                    </div>\n            \n                    <div class=\"exampleQuestion\">\n                        <style type=\"text/css\">\n                            .mjpage .MJX-monospace {\n                            font-family: monospace\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage .MJX-sans-serif {\n                            font-family: sans-serif\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage {\n                            display: inline;\n                            font-style: normal;\n                            font-weight: normal;\n                            line-height: normal;\n                            font-size: 100%;\n                            font-size-adjust: none;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            text-align: left;\n                            text-transform: none;\n                            letter-spacing: normal;\n                            word-spacing: normal;\n                            word-wrap: normal;\n                            white-space: nowrap;\n                            float: none;\n                            direction: ltr;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                            }\n\n                            .